# Coordinator request bounds

Every size and every count the coordinator accepts from the network is bounded
here, before anything reaches the database. The coordinator is reachable from the
whole internet through the tunnel, so each limit is a number a stranger cannot
move: a body larger than its route allows is refused unread, a page of a list is
never longer than the coordinator chose, and a lease never outlives two hours.

## Note
The largest body each kind of request may carry, in bytes. An attempt carries the
submitted proof document, so it may be large; a lease request or a heartbeat is a
handful of fields.

## To leaseBodyLimit () -> Int:
    Return 16384.

## To heartbeatBodyLimit () -> Int:
    Return 4096.

## To attemptBodyLimit () -> Int:
    Return 6291456.

## Note
Whether a body fits its route's limit. `length of` a text counts its bytes.

## To bodyFits (body: Text, limit: Int) -> Bool:
    Return length of body is at most limit.

## Note
A lease's time to live: fifteen minutes unless the worker asks otherwise — one
model call and one kernel run — and never under one minute or over two hours.

## To clampTtl (ms: Int) -> Int:
    If ms is at most 0:
        Return 900000.
    If ms is less than 60000:
        Return 60000.
    If ms is greater than 7200000:
        Return 7200000.
    Return ms.

## Note
How many rows one page of a list may hold: 200 unless asked, never more than 500.

## To clampLimit (n: Int) -> Int:
    If n is at most 0:
        Return 200.
    If n is greater than 500:
        Return 500.
    Return n.

## Note
Where a page of a list starts. A negative offset is the first row; an offset past
a million rows is refused as the last row anyone will page to.

## To clampOffset (n: Int) -> Int:
    If n is less than 0:
        Return 0.
    If n is greater than 1000000:
        Return 1000000.
    Return n.

## Note
Whether a text field fits: at most `maxBytes` bytes, and empty only when the field
is optional.

## To textFits (t: Text, allowEmpty: Bool, maxBytes: Int) -> Bool:
    If length of t is equal to 0:
        Return allowEmpty.
    Return length of t is at most maxBytes.

## Note
Whether a text is a lowercase hex SHA-256 digest: exactly 64 of `0-9a-f`. Every
hash the factory stores has this shape (`factory.sha256` in the schema).

## To isSha256Hex (t: Text) -> Bool:
    If length of t is not equal to 64:
        Return false.
    Repeat for b in text_bytes(t):
        If (b is at least 48 and b is at most 57) or (b is at least 97 and b is at most 102):
            Let digit be b.
        Otherwise:
            Return false.
    Return true.

## Test: coordinator bodies are bounded per route

Expect that bodyFits("abc", 3) is equal to true.
Expect that bodyFits("abcd", 3) is equal to false.
Expect that bodyFits("é", 1) is equal to false.
Expect that leaseBodyLimit() is less than attemptBodyLimit().
Expect that attemptBodyLimit() is less than 8388608.

## Test: coordinator lease lengths and pages are clamped

Expect that clampTtl(0) is equal to 900000.
Expect that clampTtl(5) is equal to 60000.
Expect that clampTtl(600000) is equal to 600000.
Expect that clampTtl(99999999) is equal to 7200000.
Expect that clampLimit(0) is equal to 200.
Expect that clampLimit(9999) is equal to 500.
Expect that clampLimit(25) is equal to 25.
Expect that clampOffset(-3) is equal to 0.
Expect that clampOffset(2000000) is equal to 1000000.

## Test: coordinator digests are lowercase hex of length sixty four

Expect that isSha256Hex("ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad") is equal to true.
Expect that isSha256Hex("BA7816BF8F01CFEA414140DE5DAE2223B00361A396177A9CB410FF61F20015AD") is equal to false.
Expect that isSha256Hex("abc") is equal to false.
Expect that isSha256Hex("") is equal to false.

## Test: coordinator text fields are empty only when optional

For all booleans allowEmpty:
    Let fits be textFits("", allowEmpty, 10).
    Expect that fits is equal to allowEmpty.
    Let longFits be textFits("abcdefghijk", allowEmpty, 10).
    Expect that longFits is equal to false.
